foreign  [Music]  as a data engineer analyst or data  scientist your main goal is most often  to transform raw data into high quality  insights and ultimately business value  wrangling that data in the form of tasks  like cleaning transforming and mapping  is frequently cited as the most time  consuming part of the process while it's  common to perform wrangling with complex  SQL scripts this approach requires a lot  of Maintenance it's difficult to  operationalize and draws Focus away from  your ultimate goal of uncovering  insights in this video we're going to  show you the Wrangler feature of cloud  data Fusion which is an interactive  visual tool that lets you operationalize  data transformation mapping and  cleansing processes and reduces time to  insights  cloud data Fusion is part of Google  Cloud which means it integrates smoothly  with the rest of our data management  processing and analytics portfolio  Wrangler has an intuitive drag and drop  interface which helps you easily build  transformations to clean and format your  data the tool allows you to test the  effects of your Transformations on a  small subset of the data so that you  gain an understanding of how they will  affect the data set as a whole  once you're happy with their  Transformations recipe you can then run  them as a pipeline within pipeline  Studio to dispatch large parallel  processing jobs on your entire data set  since Wrangler is a visual tool let's  run through an example scenario so that  you can see these features in action  in this demo we'll be cleaning and  transforming data with wrangler's  interactive UI and then creating a  transformation pipeline to ingest the  process data into bigquery  first let's head into the data Fusion UI  the tiles on the home page map to the  cloud data Fusion features such as  pipeline studio and Wrangler  from here we'll head directly to  Wrangler  on the left side you can access  pre-configured connections to your data  in this demo we're using a file located  in a Google Cloud Storage bucket this  CSV file contains a list of  Transportation passengers  if you want to work with multiple data  sources at a given time Wrangler does  provide this option  today though we're focusing on wrangling  our passenger data file  one of the first things you'll see in  the window is the column information  panel the cabin column has only 22.8  percent completion meaning it has some  rows that are missing data  to modify data inside this column or any  column click on the Arrow at the left of  the column name  using a built-in transformation you can  fill all null or empty cells with a  value you provide  after applying this transformation in  the pipeline the cabin column will be  100 complete  then you can use the change data type  function on the passenger ID column to  convert it to integer  Wrangler can also help create data  quality checks you can use a send to  error transformation to report any empty  values present in the age column to the  error collector  as you create your Transformations you  can see them collected in the far right  hand side of the UI  the transformation steps together form a  recipe  a copy of this recipe can be downloaded  so that you can apply it in the future  to other data sets as well  once your recipe is complete you can  utilize the pipelines feature of data  Fusion to apply the transformations to  your entire data set  click create a pipeline and choose batch  pipeline  this opens the studio UI  name your pipeline  then choose sync  this is the destination to which you  want your process data to flow in this  demo the sync is a table in our bigquery  data warehouse  in the properties menu you will provide  the required details to point data  Fusion to a bigquery project  data set ID  and table name  click validate to ensure the properties  are valid  back in the main Studio view you're now  ready to deploy the pipeline  click run to start execution  once the pipeline is finished you can  head over to the bigquery console to  view the destination table  its details and even run queries  we've given you a glimpse into the power  Wrangler has to help you extract more  meaningful insights from your data and  enable faster decision making we know  these are important capabilities as  businesses work to become more data  driven and data informed organizations  to try Wrangler out for yourself check  out the tutorial Linked In the  description below or reach out to your  sales representative if you have any  questions or would like to discuss how  Wrangler can help your data Journey  [Music]

